## 2. Introduction

### 2.1 Background

Online recruitment has become an important part of the job-seeking process. Government organizations, private companies, NGOs, educational institutions, and other employers frequently publish job advertisements through digital platforms.

However, the growth of online recruitment has also created opportunities for fraudulent activities. Fake recruitment advertisements may impersonate organizations, request unauthorized payments, collect personal information, distribute malicious links, or mislead applicants through false promises.

Job seekers often find it difficult to determine whether an advertisement is trustworthy, particularly when it is shared through social media or forwarded messages without an official source.

Traditional methods of verification require users to manually search official websites, compare information, check URLs, and contact organizations. These processes may be time-consuming and confusing for inexperienced users.

CircularCheck AI proposes an intelligent digital solution that combines automated analysis with verification guidance to make the job-circular checking process easier, faster, and more accessible.

### 2.2 Project Overview

CircularCheck AI will provide an integrated platform for analyzing recruitment advertisements and identifying potential warning signs.

Users will be able to:

- Submit job circular text for analysis.
- Upload screenshots and images of job advertisements.
- Upload PDF recruitment notices.
- Submit URLs for analysis.
- Receive structured AI-generated analysis reports.
- View potential fraud indicators.
- Review positive and negative verification signals.
- Check available official-source references.
- Save and revisit previous analyses.
- Report suspicious circulars.
- Explore community-reported suspicious recruitment advertisements.
- Access educational resources about employment-related scams.

The platform will combine automated AI analysis, rule-based detection, and available verification data to produce a structured assessment.

