## 3. Problem Statement

Job seekers face several challenges when evaluating the authenticity of online job advertisements.

### 3.1 Fake Recruitment Advertisements

Fraudulent advertisements may imitate legitimate organizations, government institutions, companies, NGOs, or recruitment agencies.

### 3.2 Unauthorized Payment Requests

Some suspicious recruitment advertisements may request application fees, processing charges, interview fees, training fees, or other payments through personal accounts or unofficial channels.

### 3.3 Misleading Information

Fraudulent advertisements may contain unrealistic salary claims, false recruitment promises, misleading deadlines, inconsistent job descriptions, or fabricated organizational information.

### 3.4 Suspicious URLs and Websites

Job seekers may encounter suspicious links, impersonated websites, lookalike domains, phishing pages, or websites designed to collect sensitive information.

### 3.5 Lack of Accessible Verification Tools

Many applicants do not have access to a centralized platform that can help them analyze job advertisements and understand potential warning signs in a simple and accessible manner.

### 3.6 Difficulty Understanding Risk Indicators

Even when suspicious information is present, users may not understand why a particular advertisement is potentially risky.

CircularCheck AI will address these challenges through automated analysis, transparent explanations, risk indicators, and verification guidance.

