## 10. Verification Methodology

CircularCheck AI will use multiple verification techniques where applicable.

### 10.1 Official Website Verification

The system may compare extracted information with available official websites and verified recruitment sources.

### 10.2 Domain Analysis

The system may evaluate:

- Domain structure.
- URL patterns.
- HTTPS availability.
- Lookalike domain characteristics.
- Domain-related information available through supported services.

HTTPS alone shall not be treated as evidence that a website is trustworthy.

### 10.3 Contact Information Analysis

The system may analyze:

- Email domain consistency.
- Contact number patterns.
- Presence of personal contact information.
- Contact information inconsistencies.

### 10.4 Reference Data

The system may use an internal or externally sourced reference dataset containing:

- Known official recruitment websites.
- Organization domains.
- Government recruitment portals.
- Verified contact information.
- Trusted reference URLs.

### 10.5 Verification Status

The platform will display verification statuses such as:

- Verified Against Available Source.
- Partially Verified.
- Unverified.
- Unable to Verify.

These statuses will be determined by the evidence available to the system, not by AI confidence alone.

